{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"ee3a5688c1e1101db4b99036b87d20525c6a89a400c17654d3d6873ea5f5727b","digest":{"component_or_area":"link graph / dependency recording","key_entities":["src/rebar/graph/_links.py:207","src/rebar/graph/_links.py:213","src/rebar/_lib_writes.py:615","src/rebar/_commands/composer.py:629","src/rebar/_mcp_writes.py:213","add_dependency","link_core","rebar.link","_python_leaf","link_tickets","quiet=True","redirect record"],"problem_keywords":["silent escalation","cross-subtree link","return value dropped","stdout-only channel","library caller","MCP caller"],"propositions":["add_dependency composes a redirect record for escalated cross-subtree links but emits it only to stdout, invisible to library and MCP callers who receive literal 'ok'","rebar.link() calls composer.link_core(..., quiet=True) which wraps the call in redirect_stdout/redirect_stderr, discarding the redirect record","link_tickets (MCP tool) returns 'ok' unchanged regardless of whether endpoints were escalated, providing no indication that different edges than requested were recorded","The redirect record must be returned as a value through five layers (add_dependency -> link_core -> _link -> _python_leaf -> rebar.link) rather than emitted only to stdout","quiet=True must remain in place to protect MCP stdio stream integrity, so the defect is stdout-only availability not the suppression itself"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787353083554006001,"uuid":"6c9334c2-a966-4f92-a514-4bd37e3485de"}